# `pop` is asked far more often than it pops: its loop mostly runs no turn. `kept` is no constant (`renew` gives it another list), and the loop reads it under a key that the turn itself makes. No
# loop that counts through a list looks so, nothing is tested in front of it, and a read of the variable in front of the loop would be paid at every call for nothing.
